.TH "TDDA VERSION" 1 "January 2026" "3.0" "tdda config manual"
.SH NAME
\fBtdda config\fR \- Shows config settings

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtdda config [--annotated|-a] [--current|-c] [--default|-d] [--file|-f]\fR
.br
\fBtdda config [--annotated|-a] current|default|file\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows configuration information. Use:

.PP
\fB-c\fR, \fB--current\fR, or \fBcurrent\fR for the current configuration
.br
\fB-d\fR, \fB--default\fR, or \fBdefault\fR for the default configuration
.br
\fB-f\fR, \fB--file\fR, or \fBfile\fR for the configuration file location and contents.

.PP
With no argument, it shows the current configuration.

.PP
Use \fB-a\fR or \fB--annotated\fR with any of the above to show allowed values
alongside each parameter.

.SH EXAMPLES
\fBtdda config\fR
.br
\fBtdda config -c\fR
.br
\fBtdda config -d\fR
.br
\fBtdda config -f\fR

.SH PARAMETERS
.SS \fBnull_rep\fR
Used to show nulls in some contexts.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"∅"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP Any string

.SS \fBcolour\fR
Controls whether output is colourized.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBtrue\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBengine\fR
Controls whether pandas or polars is used for CSV files by default.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"pandas"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fB"pandas"\fR, \fB"polars"\fR

.SS \fBpandas_backend\fR
Controls default backend for CSV loading etc.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"numpy_nullable"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fB"numpy_nullable"\fR (or \fB"n"\fR), \fB"pyarrow"\fR (or \fB"a"\fR), \fB"original"\fR (or \fB"o"\fR)

.SH PARAMETERS (referencetest)
.SS \fBleft_colour\fR
Colour for left (actual) side of diffs.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"red"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP A named ANSI colour (red, bright_red etc.) or an RGB hex colour with leading # such as #FF0000 for pure red. Interpreted by the rich library.

.SS \fBright_colour\fR
Colour for right (expected) side of diffs.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"green"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP A named ANSI colour (red, bright_red etc.) or an RGB hex colour with leading # such as #FF0000 for pure red. Interpreted by the rich library.

.SS \fBfailure_colour\fR
Colour used to highlight failures.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"red"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP A named ANSI colour (red, bright_red etc.) or an RGB hex colour with leading # such as #FF0000 for pure red. Interpreted by the rich library.

.SS \fBmono\fR
Use bold instead of colour for diffs.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBbw\fR
Black and white mode: no colour or bold.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBleft_prefix\fR
Prefix string for left (actual) diff lines.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"< "\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP Any string

.SS \fBright_prefix\fR
Prefix string for right (expected) diff lines.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"> "\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP Any string

.SS \fBvertical\fR
Show diffs vertically rather than side by side.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBforce_val_prefixes\fR
Always show left/right prefixes on diff lines.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBtype_checking\fR
How strictly to check types in reference test comparisons.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"strict"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fB"strict"\fR, \fB"medium"\fR, \fB"loose"\fR

.SS \fBlog_failures\fR
Log failing test IDs to file for use with tdda tag.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SH PARAMETERS (constraints)
.SS \fBinterleave\fR
Interleave pass and fail results in verify output.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBtrue\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBper_constraint\fR
Report results per constraint rather than per field.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBtrue\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBdetect_passes\fR
Include passing fields in detect output.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBtrue\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBreport_formats\fR
List of additional report formats to generate.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB[]\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP Any subset of \fB"html"\fR, \fB"md"\fR, \fB"txt"\fR, \fB"json"\fR, \fB"yaml"\fR, \fB"toml"\fR

.SS \fBwrite_all_records\fR
Write all records to detect output, not just failures.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBint_bools\fR
Use integers (0/1) rather than booleans in detect output.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBverify_required_fields\fR
Verify that all required fields are present.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP unset
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBverify_allowed_fields\fR
Verify that no fields are present outside the allowed set.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP unset
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBwrite_required_fields\fR
Discover should include the required-fields constraint.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SS \fBwrite_allowed_fields\fR
Discover should include an allowed-fields constraint.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBfalse\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SH PARAMETERS (tddadiff)
.SS \fBtype_checking\fR
How strictly to check types when comparing dataframes.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"medium"\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fB"strict"\fR, \fB"medium"\fR, \fB"loose"\fR

.SS \fBinfer_md\fR
Infer metadata when comparing dataframes with tdda diff.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fBtrue\fR
.br
\fBAllowed:\fP \fBtrue\fR, \fBfalse\fR

.SH PARAMETERS (serial)
.SS \fBmd_inpath\fR
Path(s) to search for serial metadata files; relative paths are resolved relative to the CSV file.
.br
\fBDefault:\fP \fB"./_write.serial"\fR
